                             UPDATE FROM v1.04

                              DOCUMENTATION:
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

What is NetControl for ?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
First of all Netcontrol is a TOTAL replacement for the orginal /Xnet Scripts
in your AMIXNET/SCRIPTS/ directory. This utility will solve ALL problems
with the daily /Xnet transfers. It will totally control your nettransfers,
so this scripts will not look so unproffesional for AmiExpress.
 
Requirements
~~~~~~~~~~~~
The minimum requirements for running this Utility is a full installed 
AmiExpress v3.20+ and a fully installed /Xnet v5.1+ version. If you are not
a proud owner of this two things or if you are not registered now for /Xnet5.1
this utility will be totally useless for you, because many things changed in
the release of /Xnet v5.1+

Additional Requirements:
-----------------------
AmiExpress v3.20+                ->
Acp Server v3.20+                ->
NetPack v5.1+                    ->
NetMerge v6.2+                   ->
MRUpdate v1.8+                   -> if you don`t own one of this
MSGReceipts v1.1+                -> Utilities with the correct
TERM v2.9+                       -> version number or higher then
TaskTime v1.1+                   -> this utility will not work 100%
DisplayRoute v1.2+               -> get all Utilities before using it.

Original WB Commandos needed:
---------------------------- 
C:run
C:dir
C:delete
C:copy
C:Type

Functions
~~~~~~~~~
The functions for this utility are very simple. First of all you have 2
different functions which this utility works on. You can start this utility
so that it will call out for you every day at a specified time and will
transfer all mails automatically. And the second function is the MANUAL
function. This one is for people which don`t want to let the computer call out
because of high phonebills. So you can transfer mails when ever you want by
hand and then this utility will convert all mails automatically into your
messagesbases.
 
Configuration
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The configuration of this utility is very very easy. You just have to insert
the following syntax in your CLI:
 
1> NetControl.exe CONFIG

Then this utility will prompt you for inserting some informations about your
configurated Express and /Xnet. Answer this question correctly step by step and
you will get no problem with the later automatically running of this program.
You will also be prompted for inserting information of the NETIDs you want to
call. If you are prompted for the phonenumber just insert the whole number
with the land & countrycode.
 
The other things in the configuration are very easy to manage.
 
Automatical CALLING:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If you want the NetControl automatically transfer netmails every day ,you just
have to start the NetControl once at your startup-sequence to be sure it`s
100% running if your system crashs or you make a reset.

Goto your favourite Texteditor and insert the following into your own
startup-sequence:
 
------ cut here -------
UTILS:NetControl.exe START
------ cut here -------

This will initate the Tasktime at every RESET. In this example here
it`s important to have the "NetControl.exe" program located in the UTILS:
directory.

From now on NetControl will suspend your choosen /Xnode at your favourite time
you inserted in the configuration. Then it will pack all needed netmails to
transfer and call all HostIds you inserted in the CONFIG. After the transfer
it will decrunch(merge) all downloaded netmails from your HOST and will
automatically post it in the different Conferences. This procedure will be
started again every day at the same time you choose in the Config.

Manual Transfers:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This function was included because if you call out a HOST BBS which is far
away from you which will result high phonebills.
To use this function you have to do the following step by step.
 
1. Exit the /X Node you want to call out
2. Take a Shell and start the NetControl program as follows:
 
   1> NetControl.exe LOCAL

3. Wait until NetControl will prompt you for transfering /XNetMails.
4. Start now your favourite Terminalprogram.
5. Call your HOST BBS you want to transfer mail.
6. Wait until the prompt "ANSI Graphics (Y/n)?"
7. Insert now "!--NET--!" or "@--NET--@" and press return
8. Now you will be prompted to insert your NETID.
9. Follow this prompt and insert your own NETID with the "@".
10.Now you will prompted to insert your own NetPassword you choose for this
   HOST BBS.
11.Insert this password and wait until you will be prompted to press
   return to receive the newest netmail.
12.Receive your mail and then you will be prompted if you have netmail to
   transfer or not.
13.Transfer now all NetMailFiles NetControl will list you.
14.If you are ready with uploading all Netmails just go back in the Shell 
   where NetControl was started and press return for telling NetControl that
   you are ready with all Transfers.

From now on NetControl will do all work alone and will post all netmessages in
it`s conferences.
If you have a second or more HOST BBS`s Netcontrol will go to the next HOST BBS
and will start at step 3 again.

Single-Host BBS calling
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Another included function is the Single BBS Calling. With this function you can
choose one HOST BBS you want to call automatical. This is usefull if this BBS
was busy at the specified time you called it autmatically.
 
To use this function you just have to open a shell and then insert the
following commands while /X is Awaiting Connect on that Node you choose at the
NetControl Config.
 
1> NetControl.exe <NetID>
 
You have to insert the whole netid with "@" instead of <NetID>. Then /X will 
start suspending and call this BBS automatically.
 
Help-Screen
~~~~~~~~~~~
To Open a help screen you have to start NetControl like this:
 
1> NetControl.exe ?
 
Then the following screen will appear:
 
.----------------------------------------------------------.
|       /X Net Controler v1.05 - Written by The Bird       |
|        /X Development Team - The Silent Achievers        |
`----------------------------------------------------------'

 This is a utility for AmiExpress 3.20+ & /XNet 5.1+ only!
 Copyright (c)`93 LightSpeed Technologies.

 Usage: NetControl [START]   - Initate TaskTime in Startup-Sequence
        NetControl [CONFIG]  - Start the Configuration program
        NetControl [LOCAL]   - Activate the manual Nettransfer
        NetControl [@NETID]  - Allows you to call only ONE NETcontact

This screen will list all options you have with NetControl on one page.
 
Changes to v1.01
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
After the v1.00 Release i found some bugs in the Manual Transfer Routine
